# Donburi environment variables (example)
#
# Usage:
#   cp .env.example ~/.secrets    # ~/.secrets is sourced by zsh/donburi.zsh
#   $EDITOR ~/.secrets            # fill in your real values
#   source ~/.secrets             # load now (or open a new terminal)
#   donburi meeting on            # uses these to authenticate gcalcli
#
# .env and ~/.secrets are gitignored. Do NOT commit real credentials.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Next-meeting widget (Google Calendar via gcalcli)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# gcalcli needs your OWN Google Cloud OAuth "Desktop app" client (it ships none).
# Setting these lets `donburi meeting on` authenticate without interactive prompts.
#
# Create them once:
#   1. Google Cloud Console -> create a project
#   2. Enable the Google Calendar API
#   3. OAuth consent screen -> External, app name "gcalcli", add yourself as a Test user
#   4. Credentials -> Create OAuth client ID -> Application type: Desktop app
#   5. Copy the Client ID and Client secret below
GCALCLI_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
GCALCLI_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret
